#!/usr/bin/python3
"""rq: one render queue for several Claude Code sessions on one Mac.

Strictly one heavy job at a time, first come first served. A session submits a
heavy job with `rq run`. That starts the job's own rq supervisor, detached from
the session but with its environment, cwd and sandbox, which waits for the
job's turn, runs it and records the result. `rq run` itself only watches: it
streams the job's output live and exits with the job's exit code. Stopping it
(or the session ending) does not stop the job; `rq cancel ID` does, and
`rq wait ID` watches a job again. The dispatcher (`rq daemon`) only decides
whose turn it is and serves the status page.

  rq run --name NAME (--output PATH... | --no-output) [--project P] [--estimate 90m] [--detach]
         [--again | --replace] -- COMMAND [ARGS...]
  rq light --name NAME (--output PATH... | --no-output) [--project P] [--detach] [--again | --replace]
         -- COMMAND [ARGS...]   (light work: the light queue, one at a time, at nice 10)
  rq wait ID [-n LINES]     (watch a job again: its output from here, then its exit code; at once if it ended)
  rq mine [--unwatched] [--hook]   (this session's jobs no task of it watches, results that didn't reach it)
  rq status [--json]
  rq log ID [-n LINES] [-f]
  rq cancel ID | rq pause ID | rq resume ID
  rq move ID first          (when the user says go: put a queued job next in line)
  rq move ID queue          (pause a running light job and move it to the end of the main queue)
  rq estimate ID 90m        (set or correct a job's expected duration)
  rq keep ID                (when the user says so: a light job may run longer than 5 min)
  rq start [--port 8642]    (start the dispatcher and status page detached, once per machine)
  rq daemon [--port 8642]   (the same in the foreground)

A single COMMAND argument runs through /bin/zsh -c, several run as argv. Every
job says where it writes its pictures and videos: --output PATH (-o), repeated
for several, each a file, a folder (ending in /) or a frame pattern
(renders/####.png, %04d, %d: with the zero padding the job writes), relative
to the current folder and inside the project's folder or its Claude Code
scratchpads (symlinks resolved); or --no-output. The status page shows what is
at those paths when a job's sheet is opened. An identical job (same project,
name, folder and command) that is still queued or running and that no task of
its session watches is not submitted again (if only its outputs differ, it
takes this call's): --again queues another copy, --replace first cancels the
project's jobs of that name. A job of that name from another folder or with
another command gets a note.

rq run and rq wait exit with: 0 done; the job's code if it failed, 128+n if
signal n ended it (also when it was cancelled while running, e.g. 143); 130
cancelled before it ran; 75 lost; 129 the session it reported to ended while
it watched; 128+n when the watcher itself got signal n (143 for a TaskStop,
the job carries on; the last line says which); 141 nobody read its output any
more. rq run refuses with (nothing was queued): 64 no --output and no
--no-output, both, an --output outside the project or not a picture or video,
or a --project that isn't one folder name; 65 an identical job is still queued or running and unwatched; 69 an
older dispatcher runs. 70: the job's supervisor could not start. --detach
exits 0 once the job is submitted.
"""
